@page "/docs/utilities/shimmer"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.Shimmer
<PageTitle>Shimmer - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Shimmer</h1>
            <BzBadge Variant="BadgeVariant.Secondary">Utilities</BzBadge>
            <BzBadge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">CSS only</BzBadge>
        </div>
        <p>A highlight that sweeps across something still being produced: the usual sign that a line is still being written or a step is still running. Two modes off one mechanism - <code>shimmer</code> paints text, clipping the band to the glyphs, and <code>shimmer-block</code> paints a surface, so a placeholder tile gets the same sweep. The band is derived from the element's own colour, so it reads on muted text, foreground text and a theme colour alike, in light and dark, with nothing to configure - and the text underneath stays at full strength, so a shimmering line measures for contrast exactly like a still one. <a class="text-foreground font-medium" href="docs/components/skeleton">Skeleton</a> is built on the surface mode.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(ShimmerUsageExample)"
                Setup="@null"
                Description="One class on the text. Nothing to install and nothing to register - the utilities come with the sheet Blaizio already imports into your Tailwind entry point." />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Default"
          Description="The same class over four different colours and sizes. Size the element to its text (w-fit here) so the band sweeps across the glyphs rather than across an empty box."
          Example="typeof(ShimmerDefaultExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Surface mode"
          Description="shimmer-block sweeps the element's own fill rather than its text, which is what a skeleton or a placeholder tile needs. Every knob below works on it too."
          Example="typeof(ShimmerBlockExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Colour"
          Description="shimmer-color-* replaces the band while the text keeps its own colour. Any theme colour works, and a bracketed value takes anything CSS accepts."
          Example="typeof(ShimmerColorExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Speed, spread and angle"
          Description="Duration is in milliseconds, spread is the band's width as a percentage of the sweep, angle is in degrees - 90 runs straight along the line, lower values tilt it."
          Example="typeof(ShimmerTuningExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Playback"
          Description="A single pass instead of a loop, the sweep reversed, and the opt-out that hands the text back."
          Example="typeof(ShimmerPlaybackExample)" />

    <Demo Title="In context"
          Description="On the title of a running step, and on a card heading whose body is still a set of skeletons."
          Example="typeof(ShimmerInContextExample)" />

    <section class="space-y-6">
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20">Class Reference</h2>
        <ClassTable Rows="@Classes" />
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20">Notes</h2>
        <p>The effect paints the text with a gradient (<code>background-clip: text</code>) and empties the glyphs with <code>-webkit-text-fill-color</code> rather than <code>color</code>, so the element's own colour is still readable by the gradient - that is what lets the band be derived from it. The glyphs themselves are filled by a solid <code>background-color: currentColor</code> underneath, which is what keeps the resting text at full contrast.</p>
        <p>The sweep follows the reading direction, so it runs right to left in an RTL subtree without being told. Reduced motion switches it off entirely and leaves plain text: unlike the scroll fades, this one moves on its own.</p>
        <p>It is decoration, not information. Keep the sentence itself honest ("Generating response...") so a reader who never sees the animation still knows what is happening.</p>
    </section>
</div>

@code {
    private static readonly (string, string[], string)[] Classes =
    [
        ("shimmer",
        [
            "background-color: currentColor;",
            "background-image: linear-gradient(var(--bz-shimmer-angle, 100deg), transparent calc(50% - var(--bz-shimmer-spread, 12%)), var(--bz-shimmer-highlight, color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 45%, var(--color-background))) 50%, transparent calc(50% + var(--bz-shimmer-spread, 12%)));",
            "background-size: 200% 100%;",
            "background-clip: text;",
            "-webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;",
            "animation: bz-shimmer-sweep var(--bz-shimmer-duration, 2s) linear;",
            "animation-iteration-count: var(--bz-shimmer-iterations, infinite);",
            "animation-direction: var(--bz-shimmer-direction, normal);",
        ],
        "Text mode: the glyphs stay at full strength and the band, clipped to them, is a sheen mixed towards the page behind."),

        ("shimmer-block",
        [
            "background-image: linear-gradient(var(--bz-shimmer-angle, 100deg), transparent calc(50% - var(--bz-shimmer-spread, 12%)), var(--bz-shimmer-highlight, color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 15%, transparent)) 50%, transparent calc(50% + var(--bz-shimmer-spread, 12%)));",
            "background-size: 200% 100%;",
            "animation: bz-shimmer-sweep var(--bz-shimmer-duration, 2s) linear;",
            "animation-iteration-count: var(--bz-shimmer-iterations, infinite);",
            "animation-direction: var(--bz-shimmer-direction, normal);",
        ],
        "Surface mode: the band paints over the element's own fill. What Skeleton uses."),

        ("shimmer-color-<color>",
        [
            "--bz-shimmer-highlight: <color>;",
        ],
        "The highlight colour: a theme colour (shimmer-color-primary) or a bracketed value."),

        ("shimmer-duration-<number>",
        [
            "--bz-shimmer-duration: calc(<number> * 1ms);",
        ],
        "One sweep's length in milliseconds. Defaults to 2000."),

        ("shimmer-spread-<number>",
        [
            "--bz-shimmer-spread: calc(<number> * 1%);",
        ],
        "The band's width as a percentage of the sweep. Defaults to 12."),

        ("shimmer-angle-<number>",
        [
            "--bz-shimmer-angle: calc(<number> * 1deg);",
        ],
        "The band's tilt in degrees. Defaults to 100."),

        ("shimmer-once",
        [
            "--bz-shimmer-iterations: 1;",
        ],
        "Plays a single pass instead of looping."),

        ("shimmer-reverse",
        [
            "--bz-shimmer-direction: reverse;",
            "--bz-shimmer-direction-rtl: normal;",
        ],
        "Sweeps the other way. The RTL pairing keeps one flip from cancelling the other."),

        ("shimmer-none",
        [
            "background-image: none;",
            "animation-name: none;",
            "-webkit-text-fill-color: currentColor;",
        ],
        "No sweep. Replaces shimmer or shimmer-block when both are present."),
    ];
}
